***************************** T A L Y S **************************2025 1451  183
                                                                  2025 1451  184
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2025 1451  185
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2025 1451  186
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2025 1451  187
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     2025 1451  188
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  2025 1451  189
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        2025 1451  190
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    2025 1451  191
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         2025 1451  192
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      2025 1451  193
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    2025 1451  194
stored in this data file:                                         2025 1451  195
                                                                  2025 1451  196
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2025 1451  197
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2025 1451  198
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2025 1451  199
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2025 1451  200
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2025 1451  201
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2025 1451  202
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2025 1451  203
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2025 1451  204
- Recoil data                                                     2025 1451  205
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2025 1451  206
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2025 1451  207
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2025 1451  208
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2025 1451  209
- Residual production cross sections                              2025 1451  210
                                                                  2025 1451  211
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            2025 1451  212
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        2025 1451  213
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   2025 1451  214
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                2025 1451  215
                                                                  2025 1451  216
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************2025 1451  217
